The Center for the Study of Gender and Sexuality is grateful to our faculty affiliates from across departments, divisions and schools who generously contribute their time and energies to the Center and its continued development.
 Join us as we take the evening to celebrate recent books by some of the CSGS’s amazing faculty affiliates including:
 Alexis Chema (Assistant Professor, English Language and Literature);
 Martha Feldman (Ferdinand Schevill Distinguished Service Professor, Music & Theater and Performance Studies);
 Allyson Nadia Field (Professor, Cinema and Media Studies);
 Rochona Majumdar (George V. Bobrinskoy Professor, South Asian Languages and Civilizations and Cinema and Media Studies);
 Noémie Ndiaye (Associate Professor, English and Romance Languages);
 Kaneesha Cherelle Parsard (Assistant Professor, English Language and Literature);
 Anna Schultz (Professor, Music); and
 Kris Trujillo (Assistant Professor, Comparative Literature)
 Free and open to the public.
 If you need assistance to attend, please contact tbrazas@uchicago.edu.

Claire Chm is a line dance instructor and a member of the Line Dancers of Chicago community. She and her friends are excited to bring line dancing back to Broken Hearts! Whether you have two left feet or you’re a line dancing pro, we’ve got lessons and song selections that will keep you on the dance floor!
